  "benchmark_method": {
    "requests": "Two fixed Italian code prompts, 320 generated tokens, temperature 0, seed 42, reasoning none, one stream. Throughput is total tokens / total decode time, not arithmetic mean of rates.",
    "mtp_comparisons": "Four excluded warmups, ABBA blocks of four requests: eight measurements per MTP cap. spec=3 means two predictions, spec=4 three; adaptation disabled for these controlled tests.",
    "no_mtp": "Separate fresh NVIDIA-only load with NO_MTP=1, four excluded warmups then eight measurements. The loaded-but-bypassed case retains MTP weights/buffers and has a different memory plan from complete unloading.",
    "prefill": "Real README/changelog document with distinct test identifier, ~16384 tokens actually processed, three distributed codes verified and cached follow-up.",
    "structured_output": "One short functional JSON case per mode, squares 1..20, correctness checked. Its rates are illustrative and not an eight-sample throughput benchmark."
  },
